{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c42b75827d582490","type":"text","text":"[[Melvain.canvas]]\n#Melonia ","x":-796,"y":-591,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"12ccdc220192b9a2","type":"text","text":"Gen Info\n\nThe Scholarium District is a sprawling network of floating structures where the next generation of magic users study under the divided gaze of The Round Table.\n\nThe Academy is suspended over a vast, enclosed botanical garden of sentient, highly dangerous flora.\n\nThe Ley-Line Transit: Public transport consists of glowing, physical tethers of energy spanning the quadrants. Students use simple cantrips to grip the current and glide to their destinations.\n\nAutomated Labor: Mundane tasks like sweeping and lighting lanterns are entirely handled by thousands of permanent Unseen Servants.\n\nArcane Fraternities: The student body is fiercely divided into factions like the Iron Arcanum (combat), the Aetherium Ascendant (theory/politics), and the Splicers (botanical experiments).\n","x":-520,"y":-591,"width":745,"height":410},
		{"id":"1f1e4afc756dbfea","type":"text","text":"Locations & Shops\n\nThe Central Village: The Shifting Flask (Alchemical Tavern)\nAn establishment situated in the student village where drinks are brewed using raw elemental energy. Complex illusions automatically alter the room's atmosphere to match the patrons' moods. It is a neutral zone, always loud and crowded with rival fraternity members.\n\nRun by a Human Enchanter named Jax and his Water Elemental bartender.\n\n\nConfiscated items inside: Ring of Spell Storing (modified to steal spells), a cursed luck blade.\n","x":-320,"y":340,"width":844,"height":312},
		{"id":"e763b4cd11102054","type":"text","text":"Bottom Left Quadrant (Lecture Halls): Hall 7-B (The Rotunda)\nA massive floating lecture hall that broke its tether and drifted down creating a spiral of seats that re arrange themselves every dawn stacking 8 lecture halls on top of each other.\n\nRun by a Hexblood Druid named Bram, who is missing an arm.\n","x":-1000,"y":488,"width":540,"height":164},
		{"id":"a785bd0b3195396b","type":"text","text":"Top Left Quadrant (Arenas): The Apex Sphere\nThe highest-stakes zero-gravity dueling arena. There is no artificial gravity here; combatants must push off floating debris or use spells with knockback (like Thunderwave) for propulsion. Taking bludgeoning/force damage sends you drifting until you hit a wall.\n\nOverseen by the reigning Iron Arcanum Champion: Korgoth, a Minotaur Sorcerer who uses explosive magic purely for high-speed mobility.\n","x":-1000,"y":200,"width":580,"height":240},
		{"id":"ef0143a10bf94b64","type":"text","text":"Top Right Quadrant (Faculty Spire): The Vault of Infractions\nA heavily warded, windowless stone extrusion on the side of the teachers' lounge. This is where the Master of Wards locks away confiscated contraband, banned magic items, and dangerous homebrew weapons seized from students. Access requires a faculty sigil.\n\nGuarded by \"Snitch,\" an awakened Gargoyle with a photographic memory who is aggressively loyal to the faculty and cannot be bribed with gold (but loves academic gossip).\n","x":640,"y":200,"width":720,"height":240},
		{"id":"5104d11c7f88a18f","type":"text","text":"Bottom Right Quadrant (Archives): The Paradox Wing\nA specific restricted section of the library where the bookshelves constantly rearrange themselves on a timer. The magic here is so dense that spatial reality warps, forcing researchers to solve spatial puzzles just to find a specific tome or exit.\n\nNavigated by Vel, a Kenku Diviner scribe who flawlessly mimics the grinding sound of the shifting shelves. For a fee, she will act as a guide through the maze.\n","x":640,"y":464,"width":680,"height":212}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"0fee466b846fbce7","fromNode":"1f1e4afc756dbfea","fromSide":"left","toNode":"a785bd0b3195396b","toSide":"right"},
